+R2,audit behavior,"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only creates an event dict; minisvc/api/handlers.py:13 and :20 return the event in responses; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table.","No durable audit trail exists for create or read actions despite documentation implying one.","Add audit persistence or adjust documentation and operational assumptions to match response-only events.","Backend engineer"
+R3,configuration/runtime environment,"minisvc/cli.py:7-10 calls repo.init_schema(), but minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-20 assume a ready repo without schema initialization.","HTTP deployments can fail at runtime with missing-table errors if the integrator skips the CLI bootstrap path.","Initialize schema during service startup for HTTP deployments or make repository construction enforce schema readiness.","Backend engineer or service integrator"
+R4,API input validation,"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...), with no validation or exception handling.","Malformed or missing input can cause uncaught exceptions and inconsistent client-facing failures.","Add request validation and convert storage/type errors into explicit API responses.","API/backend engineer"
+R5,readonly enforcement,"minisvc/config.py:10-14 exposes Settings.readonly, but no caller checks it before minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 invokes minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22.","Operational readonly mode is ineffective, so maintenance windows or incident controls may not prevent writes.","Enforce readonly checks in the write path, preferably before save and ideally in the repository as defense in depth.","Backend engineer"
